Hi,

I've been having some issues with seewave when working remotely, in a cluster, or using RStudio server. The packare requires rgl, which apparently depends on a graphical environment, so it is limiting the use of the package to the local computer.
I've had to resort to using old versions Is rgl necessary or is it used for a few functions?

Luis J. Villanueva

